    <item>
      <title>Basic Commands</title>
      <link>/docs/kubernetes/basic-commands/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 07 Sep 2023 16:04:48 +0200</pubDate>
      <guid>/docs/kubernetes/basic-commands/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;baseline-commands&#34;&gt;Baseline commands&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;kubectl get pods&lt;/code&gt; - check if the pods are starting correctly. You can add &lt;code&gt;| grep -c &amp;lt;deployment-name&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; to count how many pods you have at a current time. You can also filter by label: &lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;code&gt;kubectl get pods -l &#39;labelname=labelvalue&#39;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
